<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This one’s pretty neato. I’m not sure if I’d ever seen an SCP written quite like this (scratched on a wall), though I feel the general gist of this has been done before (D-Class only knowledge). Where, I’m not sure. But I like how it’s done here. Using a random throwaway SCP to actually host the real thing in-universe.</p>
<p>I do wish it had a lot more… scattered graffiti. Partway through it just doesn’t feel as… casual? As it does early on. There’s a definite different feel between the beginning/end and the middling chunk. Maybe it’s intentional, I'm not sure.</p>
<p>Pretty excellent SCP though. A+</p>
